{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-115680" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/ac782575d30a0f87e5a930ae03ef91f9c606cc03baa5b4ff9037f871a63fccd9.png)\n\nThe diagram shown above is the slope field for which of the following differential equations?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115680" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/f2ad5a7c6ea5a224583246a32e0da6de66c834f4d87be1b5bc646d3c7a678163.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-2$ and $x=4.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should equal zero on both of these lines.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that satisfy this condition are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}(4-x) \\\\ {y}^{′} & =(x+2)(x-4)^{2} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =3x(x+2)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can dismiss the equation ${y}^{′}=3x(x+2)(x-4)^{2}.$ Although the right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-2$ and $x=4,$ it also evaluates to zero when $x=0,$ which is behavior not exhibited by our slope field.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-2$ and $x=4$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-2$ | $-2<x<4$ | $x>4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↗$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nOf the two remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}(4-x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}(4-x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115680" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c209534701b5f4c071ce6a6f2e99a60e15affda0c06257cbb365a6bc6e07e2a4"} {"question" "q-115680" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115680" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-4)^{2}"] ["math" "{y}^{′}=(x+2)^{2}"] ["math" "{y}^{′}=2(x-2)(x-4)"] ["math" "{y}^{′}=3x(x+2)(x-4)"] ["math" "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}(4-x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115680" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}(4-x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/34af8d1078100aea331c300ea529d2fdefbdd31e99ee8a7946325d58a8abf680.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=7-{x}^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x+7}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{3}{x+7}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/d02883b776dbcd55c5c96347ed1a7bb0e51ef8c26e62786049b6585b878d04fb.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The solution curves have the vertical asymptote $x=-7.$\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=7-{x}^{2}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not approach $\\pm \\infty $ as $x\\to -7.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x+7}$ does *not* give the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x+7}=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(1+\\frac{7}{x})}\\to -\\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation do not become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{3}{x+7}$ gives the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{x+7}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c209534701b5f4c071ce6a6f2e99a60e15affda0c06257cbb365a6bc6e07e2a4"} {"question" "q-115754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/753554f8129ab0ed83f19e5cadefba27cb3b700818bd3a3f801c64aaf01ded70.png)\n\nIdentify the differential equation that generated the slope field above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/f26e5b61c573664f0397667aff82cfe5d918e0d22f005658862c28c53d5de748.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the solution curves have vertical asymptotes $x=2$ and $x=4.$\n\nOf the given equations, the only two that satisfy this condition are\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}=\\frac{1}{(x-2)(x-4)}\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{(x-2)(x-4)}.\n$$\n\n- Second, the slopes of the slope field become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$ \n\nOf the two remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}$ become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(1-\\frac{6}{x}+\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}})}\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}$ do *not* become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c209534701b5f4c071ce6a6f2e99a60e15affda0c06257cbb365a6bc6e07e2a4"} {"question" "q-115854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x-4}"] ["math" "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4}"] ["math" "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}"] ["math" "{y}^{′}=\\frac{x-4}{x-2}"] ["math" "{y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-115854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/f855062048a7d38b2fa6c843701a182661b2235b2042ad83fbedd600b1dd770c.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{10}(x+3)(x-2)^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{5}(x+3)(2-x)$\n- ${y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-3)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/8fdec9bda9e2bcc514e56a14a6608b2f0cb74fd0943a51c944b29cc047e02cd9.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-3$ and $x=2.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-3$ and $x=2$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{10}(x+3)(x-2)^{2}$ gives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{5}(x+3)(2-x)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ and $x=2,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-3)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-2$ and $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c209534701b5f4c071ce6a6f2e99a60e15affda0c06257cbb365a6bc6e07e2a4"} {"question" "q-120038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of those listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/1135d4a7b28f5cd1ab046f89e2882cd9074b43f95b2076b261e04003e4330c14.png)\n\nThe diagram shown above is the slope field for which of the following differential equations?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/f68f830dd6d0e6fb205bfa1ac56b1818b676089a12a5bcab46699210ba9e3191.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope field is zero along the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pm 2.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on these lines.\n\nOf the given equations, the only two that satisfy this condition are\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{3}-4x=x(x+2)(x-2),\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}={x}^{2}(2+x)(2-x).\n$$\n\n- Second, the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pm 2$ divide the plane into $4$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-2$ | $-2<x<0$ | $0<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↘$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nOf the two remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{3}-4x=x(x+2)(x-2).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}={x}^{3}-4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c209534701b5f4c071ce6a6f2e99a60e15affda0c06257cbb365a6bc6e07e2a4"} {"question" "q-120073" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120073" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{′}=2x-{x}^{3}"] ["math" "{y}^{′}=4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}"] ["math" "{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-4"] ["math" "{y}^{′}={x}^{3}+2x"] ["math" "{y}^{′}={x}^{3}-4x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"} {"question" "q-120073" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{′}={x}^{3}-4x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4feab14afe1b5a7dde3e97923c506d72796a8cce96a7e3b491f6ee0dfaa5bc"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2361 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
